🏠 Problem (House Robber)

👉 Given array: [2, 7, 9, 3, 1] num naam hai array ka
👉 Each element = paisa in a house
👉 Constraint: adjacent houses loot nahi kar sakte

👉 Goal: maximum paisa lootna
🧠 First Principle Thinking (Interview me bolna)

“At every house i, I have 2 choices:

Rob this house → then I must skip i-1
Skip this house → move to next”
🔥 Recurrence (Core Idea)

dp[i]=max(dp[i−1], nums[i]+dp[i−2])

🔍 Dry Run (VERY IMPORTANT)

Array: [2, 7, 9, 3, 1]

Step 1:
dp[0] = 2
dp[1] = max(2, 7) = 7
Step 2:
i = 2:
dp[2] = max(dp[1]=7, 9 + dp[0]=2+9=11) = 11

i = 3:
dp[3] = max(dp[2]=11, 3 + dp[1]=7+3=10) = 11

i = 4:
dp[4] = max(dp[3]=11, 1 + dp[2]=11+1=12) = 12

✅ Final Answer = 12

💡 First Principle:

“Har index pe 2 choice — pick ya skip”

Recurrence:
f(i) = max(
    nums[i] + f(i-2),   // pick
    f(i-1)              // skip
)
🔍 Dry Run (Small Part)
f(4):
  pick = 1 + f(2)
  skip = f(3)
f(2):
  pick = 9 + f(0) = 11
  skip = f(1) = 7
  => 11
f(3):
  pick = 3 + f(1) = 10
  skip = f(2) = 11
  => 11
f(4):
  pick = 1 + 11 = 12
  skip = 11
=> 12
❌ Problem:
Same calls repeat ho rahe (f(2), f(1))
Time = O(2^n)
🧠 STEP 2: TOP-DOWN (Memoization)

👉 Same recursion + cache

int f(int i, vector<int>& nums, vector<int>& dp){
    if(i < 0) return 0;
    if(i == 0) return nums[0];

    if(dp[i] != -1) return dp[i];

    int pick = nums[i] + f(i-2, nums, dp);
    int skip = f(i-1, nums, dp);

    return dp[i] = max(pick, skip);
}

⚡ STEP 3: BOTTOM-UP (Tabulation)

👉 “Recursion ko ulta socho”
👉 Small → big build karo

Core Formula (MOST IMPORTANT)

dp[i]=max(dp[i−1], nums[i]+dp[i−2])

🔍 Dry Run
nums = [2,7,9,3,1]

dp[0] = 2
dp[1] = max(2,7) = 7
i=2 → max(7, 9+2=11) = 11
i=3 → max(11, 3+7=10) = 11
i=4 → max(11, 1+11=12) = 12

👉 Answer = 12

Code:
int rob(vector<int>& nums) {
    int n = nums.size();
    vector<int> dp(n);

    dp[0] = nums[0];
    dp[1] = max(nums[0], nums[1]);

    for(int i=2;i<n;i++){
        dp[i] = max(dp[i-1], nums[i] + dp[i-2]);
    }
    return dp[n-1];
}
🚀 STEP 4: SPACE OPTIMIZED (Best)

👉 Sirf last 2 values chahiye

🔍 Dry Run
prev2 = 2
prev1 = 7

i=2 → curr = max(7, 9+2=11) = 11
i=3 → curr = max(11, 3+7=10) = 11
i=4 → curr = max(11, 1+11=12) = 12
Code:
int rob(vector<int>& nums) {
    int n = nums.size();
    if(n==1) return nums[0];

    int prev2 = nums[0];
    int prev1 = max(nums[0], nums[1]);

    for(int i=2;i<n;i++){
        int curr = max(prev1, nums[i] + prev2);
        prev2 = prev1;
        prev1 = curr;
    }
    return prev1;
}
